      "math_academy_id": "q-76082",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "What is the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $6\\le 3x+9\\le 15$ or $4x-3\\ge 5?$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by solving $6\\le 3x+9\\le 15:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & \\le 3x+9\\le 15 \\\\ -3 & \\le 3x\\le 6 \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237546/assets/ab1b1f6494c00b463e7912ab3f9710aee553e3a99484822e678494b55268e398.png)\n\nThen, we solve $4x-3\\ge 5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3 & \\ge 5 \\\\ 4x & \\ge 8 \\\\ x & \\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237546/assets/1b0700462c3957759abbe608c300fece27f92dfdb9b8c14dbeb44cc053de7784.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237546/assets/25f4136a1e248ab30fc0c01feef1e27c331553c1adcf4a1c27c133764cca1ae1.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\ge -1.$",
